<article class="env-lemma" id="0GFS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GFS">Lemma <span data-tag="0GFS">81.4.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} $ be an étale covering of algebraic spaces. The functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X_{\acute{e}tale}) \longrightarrow \text{descent data for étale sheaves wrt }\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\}   \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence of categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In Properties of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/03EB" data-tag="03EB">66.18</a> we have defined a site $X_{spaces, {\acute{e}tale}}$ whose objects are algebraic spaces étale over $X$ with étale coverings. Moreover, we have identifications $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X_{\acute{e}tale}) = \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X_{spaces, {\acute{e}tale}})$ compatible with morphisms of algebraic spaces, i.e., compatible with pushforward and pullback. Hence the statement of the lemma follows from the much more general discussion in Sites, Section <a href="/tag/04TP" data-tag="04TP">7.26</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>